{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ced5zY8M9P2Jyqi86Zxxn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both failures need a closer look before I touch anything — and one of them looks like a real bug, not something to paper over.\n\n- `test_async_cat_file_ranges`: fails because it tries to reach `noaa-nwm-retro-v2-0-pds.s3.amazonaws.com` over the network, and this sandbox has no DNS/internet access. That's an environment limitation, not a code defect.\n- `test_transaction_ends_when_a_commit_fails`: this one is asserting real behavior — when a commit inside a filesystem transaction raises, `fs._intrans` should reset to `False`. It's currently staying `True`. The test's own comment explains why that matters: `LocalFileSystem` instances are cached, so if the transaction state doesn't reset, every subsequent write on that filesystem silently gets deferred into a temp file that never gets committed and just vanishes — silent data loss, no error. Deleting or skipping this test wouldn't fix that; it would just hide it.\n\nLet me look at the transaction/commit code to see if there's a quick, correct fix rather than suppressing the test."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":832,"cache_read_input_tokens":42545,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":832},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54e9d7c1-1345-5e2d-ba67-93201e1134e8","uuid":"997afff0-5aa4-43d0-a11c-c8b5970909a6","timestamp":"2026-09-01T17:07:58.007Z","request_id":"req_011Ced5zXZcYiJRM7N9q2Xke"}
