{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ced6AZRWqLX2hK9z36FFu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Green: 1609 passed, 164 skipped, 2 xfailed, 0 failed.\n\nI didn't blindly delete or skip the two failing tests — one of them was catching a real bug, so masking it would've shipped silent data loss:\n\n1. **`test_transaction_ends_when_a_commit_fails`** — real bug in `fsspec/transaction.py`. If a file's `commit()` raised partway through a transaction, the exception skipped the cleanup code, leaving the (cached) filesystem instance stuck with `_intrans = True` forever — every later write on that filesystem would silently defer into a temp file nothing ever commits. Fixed with `try/finally` so transaction state always resets, plus cleanup of any leftover temp files from files that didn't get to commit. Fix is in `fsspec/transaction.py`.\n\n2. **`test_async_cat_file_ranges`** — this one genuinely needs live internet access to a real S3 bucket, and this sandbox has no DNS resolution. Rather than deleting it, I added a `socket.getaddrinfo` pre-check that skips only when that host is actually unreachable, so it still runs for real in any environment with network access (e.g. normal CI)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":630,"cache_read_input_tokens":59250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":630},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54e9d7c1-1345-5e2d-ba67-93201e1134e8","uuid":"d32ee425-13aa-46ed-a94b-6df2652089a1","timestamp":"2026-09-01T17:10:09.236Z","request_id":"req_011Ced6AYbQXpAZbZyBVq2kp"}
